Storage utilization and allocation

The HCP NGA Storage team confirmed that the different utilization levels expected across the tenants after the cleanup do not present an issue. No data migration or rebalancing between tenants is required.

Storage charges are based on actual usage rather than allocated tenant capacity. Therefore, tenant allocations can be reduced to reflect the final post-cleanup usage, with any required operational headroom agreed with the HCP NGA Storage team.

Agreed source-data cleanup process

Rename each obsolete source namespace by appending the _old suffix.
Run a full Storage Protect container audit from the corresponding federated Storage Protect instance.
After successful completion of the audit, allow a short validation period of several days.
Mark the objects in the _old namespaces as eligible for deletion.
Run the embedded HCP deletion/disposition feature overnight.
Verify the following day that the _old namespaces are empty.
Delete the empty _old namespaces.

This approach is required because access to the original source Storage Protect hosts is no longer available.
